    1271	### D1 — Ergodic theory / dynamical zeta functions
    1272	
    1273	**Question:** Define a dynamical system whose periodic orbits encode
    1274	primes (via the dynamical zeta function), then use Ruelle / Pollicott
    1275	results on exponential mixing to extract π(x).
    1276	
    1277	**Why frontier:** the dynamical zeta function `ζ_φ(s) = exp(Σ Z_n s^n /n)`
    1278	of an Anosov flow has poles related to its prime-orbit-counting function
    1279	in a way analogous to ζ(s). Pollicott proved exponential decay of
    1280	correlations — maybe the analogous decay for "natural" Anosov flows
    1281	admits polylog extraction.
    1282	
    1283	**Cross-domain ingredient:** smooth ergodic theory, transfer operators.
    1284	
    1285	**Concrete first step:** read Pollicott-Sharp 1998 on prime orbit
    1286	theorems. Find a flow whose prime orbits are *literally* the integer
    1287	primes. (Probably impossible — but maybe asymptotically equivalent.)
    1288	
    1289	**Failure profile:** no flow has integer primes as orbits without
    1290	encoding them externally (circular).
    1291	
    1292	**Budget:** 2 sessions.
