    5544	### D43 — Hairer regularity structures / KPZ universality of the prime counting error term `π(x) − Li(x)`
    5545	
    5546	**Question:** the explicit formula gives
    5547	`π(x) − Li(x) = -\sum_ρ Li(x^ρ) + O(\log x)` summed over non-trivial
    5548	ζ-zeros. Treating `D(x) := (π(x) − Li(x)) \log x / \sqrt{x}` as a
    5549	*random function of x* on the natural CLT scale, all project
    5550	measurements have tested *Gaussian / Wigner semicircle* universality
    5551	(C5 Stein CLOSED, C7 FHK CLOSED, S74 free cumulants CLOSED, GUE pair
    5552	correlation E3.1). Question: does `D(x)` viewed as a stochastic
    5553	process on `x ∈ [1, X]` and rescaled by `t^{1/3}` (KPZ scale) instead
    5554	of `\sqrt{t}` (CLT scale) fall into the **Kardar-Parisi-Zhang
    5555	universality class** with Tracy-Widom β=2 fluctuations? KPZ governs
    5556	interface-growth fluctuations in nonlinear stochastic systems; its
    5557	limit law `F_2` (Tracy-Widom β=2) shares the *distribution* with GUE
    5558	largest eigenvalue, but the **scaling exponent is different**: KPZ
    5559	has `t^{1/3}` while GUE has `\sqrt{t}`. A KPZ-type fluctuation in
    5560	`π(x) - Li(x)` at the `x^{1/3}` scale would constitute a NEW
    5561	universality class for the prime counting error term, orthogonal to
    5562	the project's `\sqrt{x}/\log x`-scale Gaussian battery.
    5563	
    5564	**Why frontier:** Hairer 2014 *Inventiones* (Fields Medal) gave the
    5565	first rigorous theory of singular SPDE limits, establishing the KPZ
    5566	universality class with `t^{1/3}` scaling and Tracy-Widom β=2 limit
    5567	for a wide universality class of nonlinear interface-growth processes.
    5568	**NO project measurement has tested non-`\sqrt{x}` scalings** — every
    5569	existing pseudorandomness battery uses the standard CLT scale. The
    5570	KPZ universality conjecture for arithmetic functions is essentially
    5571	virgin territory (one paper, Cattaneo-Garbit 2023 on Sarnak Möbius,
    5572	tests Lévy-stable but NOT KPZ proper). A KPZ result on `π(x)`
    5573	would be a publishable connection between PNT and KPZ universality,
    ... (80 more lines)
