    # Tracy-Widom β=2 Distribution: Key Properties
    
    ## 1. Explicit Form (Painlevé II Representation)
    
    The cumulative distribution function is expressed as:
    **F₂(s) = exp(−∫ₛ^∞ (x−s)q²(x)dx)**
    
    where q(x) satisfies the Painlevé II equation: **q″(s) = sq(s) + 2q(s)³** with boundary condition q(s) ~ Ai(s) as s → ∞.
    
    Alternatively, it's defined via the Fredholm determinant of the Airy kernel on the half-line (s, ∞).
    
    ## 2. Numerical Moments for β=2
    
    | Statistic | Value |
    |-----------|-------|
    | Mean | −1.771 |
    | Variance | 0.813 |
    | Skewness | 0.224 |
    | Excess Kurtosis | 0.093 |
    
    ## 3. Right-Tail Decay (x → +∞)
    
    The probability satisfies: **1 − F₂(x) ≈ (1/32πx^{3/2}) exp(−4x^{3/2}/3)**
    
    This represents sub-Gaussian decay dominated by the cubic exponential term.
    
    ## 4. Left-Tail Decay (x → −∞)
    
    Far more rapid decay: **F₂(−x) ≈ 2^{1/24} exp(ζ′(−1)) · x^{−1/8} · exp(−x³/12)**
    
